   568	/****************************************************************************
   569	 * Name: board_early_initialize
   570	 *
   571	 * Description:
   572	 *   If CONFIG_BOARD_EARLY_INITIALIZE is selected, then an additional
   573	 *   initialization call will be performed in the boot-up sequence to a
   574	 *   function called board_early_initialize().  board_early_initialize()
   575	 *   will be called immediately after up_initialize() and well before
   576	 *   board_early_initialize() is called and the initial application is
   577	 *   started.  The context in which board_early_initialize() executes is
   578	 *   suitable for early initialization of most, simple device drivers and
   579	 *   is a logical, board-specific extension of up_initialize().
   580	 *
   581	 *   board_early_initialize() runs on the startup, initialization thread.
   582	 *   Some initialization operations cannot be performed on the start-up,
   583	 *   initialization thread.  That is because the initialization thread
   584	 *   cannot wait for event.  Waiting may be required, for example, to
   585	 *   mount a file system or or initialize a device such as an SD card.
   586	 *   For this reason, such driver initialize must be deferred to
   587	 *   board_late_initialize().
   588	
   589	 ****************************************************************************/
